# Agent working instructions

This repository is a Deepcool LM240 USB LCD driver. The protocol source of truth is `deepcool-lm` (VID `0x3633`, PID `0x0026`, bulk OUT `0x01`, 320x240 RGB565). It is not a web app.

## Principles

- Inspect the relevant path before editing. State assumptions. Ask if the request is ambiguous.
- Make the smallest change that solves the request. Do not add abstractions, extra CLI, or refactors unless required.
- Touch only files related to the task. Do not clean up unrelated issues.
- Define a success check before editing (build, `list`/`pattern` on Windows, or a narrow command). Run that check after the first substantive edit.
- If unsure, say so. Do not silently choose a risky USB or driver-binding interpretation.

## Scope stop

Before editing, estimate files, components, and validation.

If more than 5 files will change, stop and present a plan first. Skip that stop when the user already asked to implement a small, named change; name the files and proceed.

## Inspection

Default to locating the relevant files and functions. Do not scan the whole repo. Use CodeGraph when more than 3 files, a shared USB helper, or impact is unclear. After a multi-file edit, run `codegraph sync .`.

## Validation

Use the narrowest check: `dotnet build` for the Windows PoC, a direct run of `deepcool-lm` changes on Linux, or the Windows LCD `pattern` command. If you cannot run it, say why and give the exact command.

## After changes

Report what changed, why, how it was validated, and remaining risk. No drive-by edits.
